#version 450

layout(local_size_x = 32, local_size_y = 1, local_size_z = 1) in;

layout(set = 0, binding = 0, std430) buffer Output {
   uint values[];
} output_buffer;

/* DOES NOT CURRENTLY ENCODE -- retained as an encodability regression test.
 *
 * Intended to settle whether "coverage" is a lane count at all.
 *
 * Across the probes, how many elements get written tracks the store's
 * index_reg field, not anything about concurrency:
 *
 *   cover/min/count  index_reg=0x0, addr_mode=0x54  ->  1 element
 *   lid              index_reg=0x4, addr_mode=0x54  ->  8 elements
 *   full             index_reg=0x0, addr_mode=0x55  ->  8 elements (different form)
 *
 * and in every failing case a register the store depends on is also written by
 * something scheduled after the value was computed -- for lid the interloping
 * frame_markers write r4, which is exactly the register its store names as the
 * index.
 *
 * This shader removes the thing contending for those registers. The addend is
 * SMALL, so iadd2 carries it as its 8-bit inline immediate (srcB_imm, K in
 * [0,255] encoded as K<<1) instead of the mov_imm + n2_op6 pair that every
 * other probe needs to materialise a 32-bit literal -- and it is that pair
 * which writes the register the store names as its index. So nothing is
 * scheduled between the index computation and the store.
 *
 * All three attempts at a small-or-absent constant are refused by the AGX3
 * packer with VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT:
 *
 *   values[l] = 0xcafe0000u   (bare literal, local-id index)   -> -8
 *   values[l] = l             (no arithmetic at all)           -> -8
 *   values[l] = l + 1u        (small inline-immediate addend)  -> -8
 *
 * while values[l] = 0x44440000u + l encodes. So a 32-bit literal that has to
 * be materialised by mov_imm + n2_op6 is currently the ONLY way to feed a
 * store -- which is unfortunate, because that pair is exactly what writes the
 * register the store names as its index.
 *
 *   32 elements holding 1..32 -> every lane runs and indexes correctly. There
 *                                is no coverage bug; the earlier counts were
 *                                lanes colliding on a clobbered index.
 *   fewer                     -> a real limit on how many lanes execute, and
 *                                the index-clobber theory is dead.
 *
 * Values are 1..32, all distinct and none equal to the 0xa5a5xxxx prefill.
 */
void
main()
{
   uint l = gl_LocalInvocationID.x;
   output_buffer.values[l] = l + 1u;
}
